  "limitations": [
    "No complete from-zero run with a fixed 72 runners was measured. These are planning estimates, not measured completion times or confidence intervals.",
    "The historical reward curve used 16, 32, 48 and then 72 runners; it must not be relabeled as a fixed-72-runner observation.",
    "The 103-150 window has a later-policy workload than early training. Extrapolation repeats that observed stage average for every requested step.",
    "Sequence lengths, reference-logprob cost, sampling staleness, serving contention and future retained state can change with policy evolution and concurrency. Matching model, data, code, hardware and configuration is required for this estimate to be informative.",
    "All 103-250 steps averaged 22.0936 minutes for read+train, and steps 221-250 averaged 37.0994 minutes. Do not extrapolate the selected stage rate to a 250-step run.",
